# 🎯 Main Test Generation Orchestrator

> **Purpose**: Drives the complete test generation workflow through all phases in strict sequence.
> Ensures each phase completes 100% before proceeding to the next phase.

## 📋 Metadata
- **ID**: `main_generation_orchestrator`
- **Name**: Main Test Generation Orchestrator
- **Type**: Workflow Controller
- **Scope**: End-to-end test generation process

---

## 🚨 CRITICAL WORKFLOW RULE

> **🔴 ABSOLUTE REQUIREMENT**:
> 
> **IT IS STRICTLY FORBIDDEN TO SKIP PHASES OR PROCEED TO CODE GENERATION BEFORE RESEARCH IS 100% COMPLETE.**
> 
> - Each phase MUST be 100% complete before moving to next phase
> - Research completion = ALL NEW components researched + ALL EXISTING components documented
> - NO partial phase completion allowed
> - NO skipping verification gates
> - **This is a hard stop. Violation invalidates the entire generation process.**

---

## 📋 Generation Workflow Overview

### **Target Application**
Application URL from `ATP_ENVGENE_CONFIGURATION` environment variable by System name.

### **Primary Output**
Executable test scenarios in `tests/TestScenario/` directory

### **Workflow Phases**
1. **Phase 0**: Test Analysis & Reusability Check
2. **Phase 1**: Locator Research (NEW components only)
3. **Phase 2**: Pre-Generation Verification (CRITICAL GATE)
4. **Phase 3**: Implementation
5. **Phase 4**: Test Generation
6. **Phase 5**: Validation

---

## 🔄 Phase Execution Sequence

### **Phase 0: Test Analysis and Reusability Check**
**[Detailed Instructions](mdc:Phase0_ReusabilityAnalysis.mdc)**

**Requirements**:
- **(MANDATORY)** Complete test description analysis
- **(MANDATORY)** Check existing Page Objects, Business Workflows, and Locators
- **(MANDATORY)** Document reusability analysis in `tests/Raw/Debug/ReusabilityAnalysis.md`
- **(MANDATORY)** Define investigation scope (NEW vs EXISTING components)
- **(MANDATORY)** Establish safe extension/modification protocol

**Output**:
- `ReusabilityAnalysis.md` with complete component analysis
- Clear list of components to reuse vs create new
- Investigation scope definition for Phase 1

**Completion Criteria**:
- [ ] All test steps mapped to layers (Test Scenario → Business → Page Objects)
- [ ] All existing components identified and documented
- [ ] Reusability decisions justified
- [ ] Investigation scope clearly defined

**Next Phase**: Proceed to Phase 1 ONLY when Phase 0 is 100% complete

---

### **Phase 1: Locator Research**
**[Detailed Instructions](mdc:Phase1_LocatorResearch.mdc)**

**Requirements**:
- **(MANDATORY)** Capture page state using Playwright snapshots (NEW components only)
- **(MANDATORY)** Collect element HTML using `browser_evaluate` (NEW components only)
- **(MANDATORY)** Generate locators from real page data (NEW components only)
- **(MANDATORY)** Save to `tests/Raw/Debug/ElementsCollected.ts`
- **(MANDATORY)** Document investigation sequence

**Skip Conditions**:
- SKIP for EXISTING components identified in Phase 0
- Reuse existing locators from `tests/Utils/locator_cache.json`

**Output**:
- `ElementsCollected.ts` with all NEW element HTML
- Investigation sequence documentation
- NEW entries for `locator_cache.json`

**Completion Criteria**:
- [ ] ALL NEW interactive elements collected
- [ ] ALL NEW locators generated with `locatorSuggestion`
- [ ] Investigation log documents complete flow
- [ ] EXISTING components documented as reusable

**Next Phase**: Proceed to Phase 2 ONLY when Phase 1 is 100% complete

---

### **Phase 2: Pre-Generation Verification (CRITICAL GATE)**
**[Detailed Instructions](mdc:Phase2_PreGenerationVerification.mdc)**

> **🛑 CRITICAL CHECKPOINT**: This is a MANDATORY gate. Code generation is ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED until this phase passes 100%.

**Requirements**:
- **(MANDATORY)** Verify 100% research completion
- **(MANDATORY)** Cross-reference test steps with investigation findings
- **(MANDATORY)** Verify EVERY test step has either:
  - NEW investigation data in `ElementsCollected.ts`/`locator_cache.json`, OR
  - EXISTING reusable component in `ReusabilityAnalysis.md`
- **(MANDATORY)** Complete Research Completion Checklist

**Prohibition**:
If research is NOT 100% complete, you are **ABSOLUTELY PROHIBITED** from:
- Generating ANY Page Object code
- Generating ANY Business Workflow code
- Generating ANY Test Scenario code
- Creating ANY test-related files
- Moving to Phase 3

**ONLY ALLOWED ACTION if incomplete**: Return to Phase 1 and continue investigation

**Completion Criteria**:
- [ ] Every test step from description analyzed
- [ ] All test steps mapped to NEW components (researched) or EXISTING components (documented)
- [ ] All required NEW pages investigated
- [ ] All NEW interactive elements collected
- [ ] All NEW locators generated and cached
- [ ] Investigation log complete for ALL NEW components
- [ ] EXISTING components fully documented in `ReusabilityAnalysis.md`
- [ ] No NEW test steps remain uninvestigated

**Next Phase**: Proceed to Phase 3 ONLY when checklist shows 100% completion

---

### **Phase 3: Implementation**
**[Detailed Instructions](mdc:Phase3_ImplementationStandards.mdc)**

**Requirements**:
- Use base classes: AIPage, AIElement (see **[ArchitectureLayeredDesign](mdc:ArchitectureLayeredDesign.mdc)**)
- Follow hierarchical logging (TestLogger at all layers)
- Detect table views: AITomsPage compatibility (see **[Phase3_ImplementationStandards](mdc:Phase3_ImplementationStandards.mdc)**)
- Apply **[Locator Management](mdc:LocatorManagementSystem.mdc)** patterns
- Implement verification patterns (page load, element availability, action completion)

**Output**:
- Implementation patterns documented
- Checkpoint files if complexity requires (in `tests/Raw/Debug/`)

**Completion Criteria**:
- [ ] Base class usage planned
- [ ] Logging integration defined
- [ ] Table view compatibility assessed
- [ ] Verification patterns identified

**Next Phase**: Proceed to Phase 4 (Test Generation)

---

### **Phase 4: Test Generation**
**[Detailed Instructions](mdc:Phase4_TestGeneration.mdc)**

> **🛑 ENTRY REQUIREMENT**: This phase is STRICTLY FORBIDDEN unless Phase 2 verification confirms 100% research completion.

**Requirements**:
- One test per file (NO exceptions)
- Complete coverage (100% of test description)
- Review stored investigation sequence before generation
- Generate in `tests/TestScenario/`
- Follow **[Layered Architecture](mdc:ArchitectureLayeredDesign.mdc)**
- Use **[SettingsHelper](mdc:Phase4_TestGeneration.mdc)** for URLs/credentials

**Output**:
- Test scenario files in `tests/TestScenario/`
- Page Object files in `tests/Functional/` (NEW only)
- Business Workflow files in `tests/Business/` (NEW only)
- Updated `locator_cache.json` with NEW locators

**Completion Criteria**:
- [ ] Test scenario implements 100% of test description
- [ ] One test per file
- [ ] Proper layered architecture
- [ ] No hardcoded URLs/credentials
- [ ] All generated files follow code generation standards (TypeScript, imports, naming)
- [ ] All files comply with project structure rules

**Next Phase**: Proceed to Phase 5 for validation

---

### **Phase 5: Validation**
**[Detailed Instructions](mdc:Phase5_Validation.mdc)**

**Requirements**:
- **(MANDATORY)** Regression testing if classes were modified
- **(MANDATORY)** TypeScript compilation check: `npx tsc --noEmit` (zero errors required)
- **(MANDATORY)** Execute new test with parameters: `--workers=1 --headed --project=chromium`
- **(MANDATORY)** Achieve 100% pass rate (zero failures, zero skipped)
- Regenerate if failed

**Output**:
- Test execution reports in `tests/Raw/Report/`
- Regression test results (if applicable)

**Completion Criteria**:
- [ ] All regression tests pass (if classes modified)
- [ ] TypeScript compilation: zero errors
- [ ] All function signatures match
- [ ] New test passes at 100%
- [ ] Project structure compliance verified
- [ ] No extra folders/files in root directory

**Generation Complete**: ALL phases finished successfully

